Subject: [PATCH] Reclassify configured addresses as data (data_funcs, data_ranges)

Tekken 2's game.toml lists three ranges of its text segment that hold
tables, not code ([recompiler] data_ranges), because data words there
decode as JAL and seed false functions. psxrecomp does not read those keys,
so this patch adds them:

- [recompiler] data_funcs (addresses) and data_ranges (half-open
  [start, end) pairs) in config_loader.
- psxrecomp-game marks every function starting inside them as data after
  each discovery pass and never promotes a candidate entry inside them.
- A data function is emitted as a fail-closed psx_unknown_dispatch stub,
  before alias grouping, so a data host gets no alias group, its aliases
  are not materialized and its CFG is empty.

Applied last, so patches 0001-0021 apply to upstream psxrecomp unchanged.

---
